IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 8 (1 of 3): regulations 24 to 28 (National Insurance credits: Chapter 1,
-- general, and Chapter 2, credits for a pre-commencement qualifying year).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- A National Insurance "credit" is a week treated as if contributions (or earnings) had
-- been paid, so that the week counts towards a "qualifying year" for the state pension.
-- Not among the inputs, so taken as plain inputs below:
--   * what a "qualifying year", "pre-commencement qualifying year" and "post-commencement
--     qualifying year" are (sections 2(4) and 4(4) of the 2014 Act);
--   * the "qualifying earnings factor", "earnings factors" and the "lower earnings limit"
--     (the 1992 Act and the figures it sets for each year);
--   * the contents of the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975, which regulations 26
--     and 27 apply on assumptions.
-- A week is named by its first day. A tax year starts on 6 April (fork F3).

§ `Part 8: National Insurance Credits`

§§ `Chapter 1: General (regulations 24 and 25)`

§§§ `Regulation 24: interpretation`

-- Paragraph (1) defines words used in this Part. Each definition either points to the
-- 2014 Act, the 1975 Regulations or another Act (not inputs) or fixes a name, so it is
-- inert here: "year" means a tax year (spr-dates.l4, F3).

-- Gloss: no credit under Chapter 3 for any day, or for any event, before 6 April 2016.
-- src:319 | (2) Nothing in Chapter 3 is to be construed as entitling any person to be credited with earnings or contributions for any day or in respect of any event occurring before 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 24(2) (src:319)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 can credit the day` day MEANS
    day AT LEAST YMD 2016 4 6

§§§ `Regulation 25: general provisions relating to the crediting of earnings or contributions`

DECLARE CreditChapter IS ONE OF
    `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)`
    `Chapter 3 (a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year)`

-- Gloss, paragraph (3): a week that falls partly in one tax year and partly in the next is
-- counted in the year in which it begins.
-- src:325 | (3) Where under this Part a person is entitled to be credited with earnings or a contribution in respect of a week that falls partly in one tax year and partly in another, that week is to be treated as falling in the year in which it begins and not in the following year.
@ref Regulation 25(3) (src:325)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    `the tax year in which the day falls` `the first day of the week`

-- Gloss, paragraph (1): Chapter 2 is for credits in respect of a pre-commencement
-- qualifying year, Chapter 3 for any other. The line is drawn at 6 April 2016 (the tax
-- year 2015 is the last before it): this agrees with regulation 28(3) ("ending before 6
-- April 2016") and regulation 33(3) ("beginning on or after 6 April 2016"); the 2014 Act
-- definitions are not inputs (fork F28).
-- src:321 | (1) For the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act—
-- src:322 | (a) Chapter 2 makes provision for crediting earnings or contributions in respect of a pre-commencement qualifying year;
-- src:323 | (b) Chapter 3 makes provision for crediting earnings or contributions in respect of a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year.
@ref Regulation 25(1) (src:321-323)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A CreditChapter
`regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    IF `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` `the first day of the week` LESS THAN 2016
    THEN `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)`
    ELSE `Chapter 3 (a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year)`

-- Gloss, paragraph (2): a person who would be credited for a year (or a week in it) is
-- credited only as much as is needed to make the year a qualifying year. How much is
-- needed is the qualifying earnings factor less what the person already has for the
-- year, and never below nothing.
-- src:324 | (2) Where under this Part a person would, but for this paragraph, be entitled to be credited with any earnings or contributions for a year, or in respect of any week in a year, that person is only to be credited to the extent necessary to make that year a qualifying year.
@ref Regulation 25(2) (src:324)
GIVEN `the amount the person would be credited with for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings factors the person already has for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` `the amount the person would be credited with for the year` `the earnings factors the person already has for the year` `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` MEANS
    IF needed LESS THAN `the amount the person would be credited with for the year`
    THEN needed
    ELSE `the amount the person would be credited with for the year`
    WHERE
        needed MEANS
            IF `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` GREATER THAN `the earnings factors the person already has for the year`
            THEN `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` MINUS `the earnings factors the person already has for the year`
            ELSE 0

§§ `Chapter 2: Crediting earnings or contributions in respect of a pre-commencement qualifying year (regulations 26 to 28)`

§§§ `Regulations 26 and 27: credits under the 1975 Regulations; credits for parents and carers`

-- Gloss: the person is credited with what they WOULD have been entitled to under the
-- Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975 for a Category A retirement pension, if the
-- amendment made by paragraph 55 of Schedule 12 to the 2014 Act had not come into force
-- and the person attained pensionable age on 6 April 2016. Those Regulations are not an
-- input, so what the person would have been entitled to on those two assumptions is.
-- Chapter 2 is for a year before 2016; for a later year the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:328 | A person is to be credited with the earnings or contributions to which the person would have been entitled under the 1975 Regulations for the purposes of entitlement to a Category A retirement pension had—
-- src:329 | (a) the amendment made by paragraph 55 of Schedule 12 to the 2014 Act (which limits Category A retirement pensions to people who reach pensionable age before 6th April 2016) not come into force, and
-- src:330 | (b) the person attained pensionable age on 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 26 (src:328-330)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the earnings or contributions the person would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations on the assumptions in regulation 26(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 26: the earnings or contributions credited under the 1975 Regulations` `the first day of the week` `the earnings or contributions the person would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations on the assumptions in regulation 26(a) and (b)` MEANS
    IF `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` `the first day of the week` EQUALS `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)`
    THEN JUST `the earnings or contributions the person would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations on the assumptions in regulation 26(a) and (b)`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Gloss: the same for a Class 3 contribution to which the person would have been
-- entitled under section 23A of the 1992 Act (credits for relevant parents and carers).
-- src:332 | A person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution to which the person would have been entitled under section 23A of the 1992 Act (contributions credits for relevant parents and carers), or regulations made under that section, for the purposes of entitlement to a Category A retirement pension had—
-- src:333 | (a) the amendment made by paragraph 55 of Schedule 12 to the 2014 Act (which limits Category A retirement pensions to people who reach pensionable age before 6th April 2016) not come into force, and
-- src:334 | (b) the person attained pensionable age on 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 27 (src:332-334)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the Class 3 contribution the person would have been entitled to under section 23A of the 1992 Act on the assumptions in regulation 27(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 27: the Class 3 contribution credited for parents and carers` `the first day of the week` `the Class 3 contribution the person would have been entitled to under section 23A of the 1992 Act on the assumptions in regulation 27(a) and (b)` MEANS
    IF `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` `the first day of the week` EQUALS `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)`
    THEN JUST `the Class 3 contribution the person would have been entitled to under section 23A of the 1992 Act on the assumptions in regulation 27(a) and (b)`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§§ `Regulation 28: credits for spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces (Chapter 2)`

DECLARE ForcesSpouseFacts HAS
    `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
    `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is accompanying the member of Her Majesty's forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application to be credited has been received by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made in respect of a past period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:337 | (2) The conditions are that the person—
-- src:338 | (a) is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty’s forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation, and
-- src:339 | (b) is accompanying the member of Her Majesty’s forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State.
@ref Regulation 28(2) (src:337-339)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 28(2): the conditions are satisfied` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation`
    AND facts's `the person is accompanying the member of Her Majesty's forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State`

-- Gloss: the regulation is for a week in a tax year that began on or after 6 April 1975
-- and ended before 6 April 2016, for which the member's earnings factors exceed the
-- qualifying earnings factor.
-- Paragraph (4)(b) speaks of "a woman" who has an election in force; the two facts are one
-- input here (fork F29).
-- src:340 | (3) This regulation applies to a week which falls within a year beginning on or after 6th April 1975 and ending before 6th April 2016 for which the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty’s forces exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
@ref Regulation 28(3) (src:340)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 28(3): the regulation applies to the week` facts MEANS
        `the first day of the tax year` taxYear AT LEAST YMD 1975 4 6
    AND `the last day of the tax year` taxYear LESS THAN YMD 2016 4 6
    AND facts's `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` GREATER THAN facts's `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    WHERE
        taxYear MEANS `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (facts's `the first day of the week`)

-- src:341 | (4) Paragraph (1) does not apply to—
-- src:342 | (a) a person in respect of a week in which the person is entitled to be credited with earnings under—
-- src:343 | (i) regulation 7A (credits for carer’s allowance or carer support payment),
-- src:344 | (ii) regulation 8A (credits for unemployment),
-- src:345 | (iii) regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work), or
-- src:346 | (iv) regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty’s forces),
-- src:347 | of the 1975 Regulations; or
-- src:348 | (b) a woman in respect of a week in any part of which an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force.
@ref Regulation 28(4) (src:341-348)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 28(4): paragraph (1) does not apply` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations`
    OR facts's `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week`

-- Gloss, paragraphs (5) and (6): no credit without an application, for a past period, on
-- an approved form or in a manner the Secretary of State accepts, with the information
-- the Secretary of State or Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs specify.
-- src:349 | (5) A person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (1) unless an application to be so credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6).
-- src:350 | (6) An application under paragraph (5) may only be made in respect of a past period and must—
-- src:351 | (a) be on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in such manner as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances, and
-- src:352 | (b) include such information as may be specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs.
@ref Regulation 28(5) and (6) (src:349-352)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 28(5) and (6): a valid application has been received` facts MEANS
        facts's `an application to be credited has been received by the Secretary of State`
    AND facts's `the application is made in respect of a past period`
    AND facts's `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient`
    AND facts's `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`

-- src:336 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a person who satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2) for any part of a week to which this regulation applies is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of that week.
@ref Regulation 28(1) (src:336)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 28(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` facts MEANS
        `regulation 28(2): the conditions are satisfied` facts
    AND `regulation 28(3): the regulation applies to the week` facts
    AND NOT (`regulation 28(4): paragraph (1) does not apply` facts)
    AND `regulation 28(5) and (6): a valid application has been received` facts
